; Three tall columns with open air between them and no floor at all across the
; middle. Every crossing is a committed swing over a fall, so the stage turns
; position itself into the contested thing: standing on a column top is safe
; and attacking off it is not. The opposite bargain to Gauntlet, where the
; ground is continuous and the ceiling is what constrains you.
;
; Eased slightly (issue #59): the crossing was near impossible for most
; weapons. The columns were 120 px wide at x = +-360, a 240 px gap: the
; staff's whole reach, so only the staff could hook the next top and
; everything else had to fling blind. Now they are 140 px wide at x = +-320,
; a 180 px gap, and the outer spawns moved in with their columns. That is
; still past the pickaxe's 150 px standing reach, so every crossing is still
; a committed swing, but a modest hop now puts the next top in hook range.
; A throwaway headless probe (random fling programs from the take-off top)
; had the pickaxe landing it about 3.5x as often (0.9% -> 3.2%, the staff's
; old rate) and the dagger about 7x (0.1% -> 0.7%). Heights are unchanged
; and there is still no floor.

; Backdrop (issue #117): canyon.
[node name="Pillars" type="Node2D"]
script = ExtResource("1")
background_sky_top = Color(0.16, 0.12, 0.18, 1)
background_sky_bottom = Color(0.3, 0.22, 0.2, 1)
background_silhouette = Color(0.18, 0.12, 0.11, 1)
